# Angular templates

---

## Scope

- Applies to: `**/*.component.html`

## Conventions

- Always use separate `.html` files in Angular components, do not use inline templates.
- Use semantic HTML with proper accessibility attributes
- Apply Tailwind classes with `crss:` prefix
- when styling text elements inside of material layout components, add a <h1>, <h2>, <h3>, <h4>, <h5>, <h6>, <span> or <p> element as appropriate and then style the element with the tailwind classes to avoid getting overridden by the material styles.
- Use Angular control flow (`@if`, `@for`) instead of structural directives
- if a signal is used in the template multiple times you may use the @let syntax to declare the variable at the top of the template and then use it multiple times in the template.

## Reference files

- @libs/quaestor/ops-command/feature/process-list/src/lib/process-list/process-list.component.html for a good example of media breakpoints and using signal stores directly in the template.
